  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>In the western districts of Toulon, near the Pont du Las, the Parc des Cèdres offers a green space of 0.66 hectare (about 6,600 m² according to the city of Toulon), with a playground and a boules court in addition to the dog area. A modest-sized neighbourhood park.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The park is among the dog areas in the municipal document "Toulon, ville amie des chiens" (published online in November 2025), which reminds visitors that a leash and picking up waste are compulsory throughout the municipality, including in dog areas. The document gives no details on opening times or the size of the dog area; a directory lists the park as open from 9am to 7pm, to be confirmed with the town hall. The modest-sized park suits a quiet stroll rather than a big sporty outing.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: a neighbourhood spot for a green break, with no need to plan a whole afternoon.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The western districts of Toulon and the Pont du Las area are right next door, handy for fitting this break into an urban walk.</p>
    </div>

